From b66a4288bc31e8b019d8b1ee39b4771535c79785 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:02:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] hexagonrpcd: listener: dispatch method IDs above 30

The method ID in the scalars only has 5 bits. Remote processors call
methods with higher IDs as method 31 and pass the actual method ID as
the first input number. This is why apps_std_stat (31) already has an
extra input number.

Read the actual method ID for method 31, so that methods like
apps_std_frename (33) can be implemented.

Signed-off-by: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 hexagonrpcd/listener.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
index 81ef614..b070b56 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
@@ -285,6 +285,14 @@ static int invoke_requested_procedure(size_t n_ifaces,
 		return 1;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Method IDs above 30 do not fit in the scalars. The remote processor
+	 * sends them as method 31 with the actual method ID as the first input
+	 * number, which the method definition must account for.
+	 */
+	if (method == 31 && REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc) > 0 && decoded[0].s >= 4)
+		method = ((const uint32_t *) decoded[0].p)[0];
+
 	if (method >= ifaces[handle]->n_procs) {
 		fprintf(stderr, "Unsupported method: %u (%08x)\n", method, sc);
 		*result = AEE_EUNSUPPORTED;
-- 
